8. DB Design

Design the team configuration schema properly for the future.

Today we may have only these fields, but this application will continue to evolve and support around 25 teams with many users.

The DB design should therefore:

* support multiple teams cleanly;
* support multiple values such as namespaces, branch overrides, excluded components, etc.;
* be easy to extend with future configuration;
* avoid unnecessary duplication;
* allow complete editing from UI;
* maintain clear separation between common configuration and team-specific configuration.

Think about this as a rapidly evolving application, not a one-time static configuration table.

